    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for the Zurich Zebras centers on exploiting favorable matchups against shaky pitching, with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) headlining our strategy as the day's elite play. His high score is driven by a massive park boost and the aggressive targeting of the opponent\u2019s slow delivery, which provides a high-probability environment for him to swipe bags\u2014a critical priority given our focus on SB scarcity. **Trea Turner** (75.29) and **Kyle Schwarber** (71.49) also command premium status, both benefiting from an inviting matchup against Singer, where their combined power and lineup positioning provide the highest projected floor for run production and HR potential.\n\nWhile **Casey Schmitt** (63.92) and **Caleb Durbin** (61.82) are locked in as strong starts, we are closely monitoring the weather risk surrounding **Lars Nootbaar** (42.24). His score is depressed by a difficult matchup against Henderson and a 38% rain probability; if the weather clears, his platoon advantage against the right-hander keeps him viable, but he remains the most volatile piece of our starting nine. **Luke Raley** (55.73) and **Chase Meidroth** (42.16) fell into the marginal category today due to their struggles against elite-level arms like Sandoval; however, with no active bench reinforcements like **Yordan Alvarez** or **Christian Yelich** available due to team off-days and roster status, we must accept the risk to preserve our daily game caps. **Junior Caminero** (61.45) and **Carson Benge** (60.28) round out our lineup, both benefiting from favorable winds and top-half-of-the-order assignments, keeping the Zebras well-positioned for a high-efficiency offensive performance.",
